---
import {readFile} from 'node:fs/promises';
import {validatePair,DATA_URL,MANIFEST_URL,METRICS,PRIMARY,VIEWS,fmt,evidence,interval,studyLabel} from '../lib/nfl-comparison';
const data = await validatePair(await readFile('public'+DATA_URL),await readFile('public'+MANIFEST_URL));
const players=data.rows.filter(r=>r.season===2023);
---
<nfl-comparison data-state="loading">
  <section aria-labelledby="nfl-comparison-heading">
    <h2 id="nfl-comparison-heading">Compare quarterbacks</h2>
    <p class="scope">20 matched passers · 2023 and 2024 regular seasons · observed values in native units</p>
    <p class="availability" id="nfl-availability" role="status" aria-live="polite">Checking the reviewed comparison data. The full tables below work without JavaScript.</p>
    <button type="button" data-retry hidden>Retry verified data</button>
    <div class="player-controls">
      <label for="nfl-player-a">QB A · filled circle<select id="nfl-player-a" name="nfl-player-a" data-a disabled>{players.map(r=><option value={r.player_key}>{r.observed_name}</option>)}</select></label>
      <label for="nfl-player-b">QB B · open diamond<select id="nfl-player-b" name="nfl-player-b" data-b disabled>{players.map((r,i)=><option value={r.player_key} selected={i===1}>{r.observed_name}</option>)}</select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="shared-controls">
      <label for="nfl-season">Season<select id="nfl-season" name="nfl-season" data-season disabled><option value="2023">2023</option><option value="2024">2024</option></select></label>
      <label for="nfl-view">View<select id="nfl-view" name="nfl-view" data-view disabled>{Object.entries(VIEWS).map(([key,v])=><option value={key}>{v.title}</option>)}</select></label>
      <label for="nfl-metric">Measure<select id="nfl-metric" name="nfl-metric" data-metric disabled>{PRIMARY.map(f=><option value={f}>{METRICS[f].label}</option>)}<option value="composition" hidden>Recorded composition</option><option value="study" hidden>All study associations</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <p class="control-note" data-control-note>Both players share the selected season and measure.</p>
    <figure class="comparison-figure" aria-labelledby="nfl-view-heading">
      <h3 id="nfl-view-heading" data-view-heading>Player comparison</h3>
      <p data-description>{VIEWS.compare.description}</p>
      <p class="identities" data-identities></p>
      <p class="unit" data-unit></p>
      <p class="plot-note" data-uncertainty></p>
      <div data-chart-host class="chart-host"><svg hidden data-plot role="img" aria-labelledby="nfl-plot-title nfl-plot-description"></svg></div>
      <figcaption>Each measure uses one fixed scale across the full cohort and both years, including available marginal limits. Zero reference lines appear where zero lies on that scale. Missing evidence stays unavailable. Players are listed by source ID, without a performance ordering.</figcaption>
      <details class="composition-key"><summary>Composition patterns</summary><p>Solid green: other D passes. Forward hatch: sacks. Sand: scrambles. Backward hatch: non-scramble runs. Read exact counts and percentages in the view table.</p></details>
    </figure>
    <details open class="evidence-table"><summary>Data behind this view</summary><div class="table-scroll" data-view-table role="region" aria-label="Data for the selected view" tabindex="0"><p>Use the complete tables below while the interactive view loads.</p></div></details>
    <details class="complete-table"><summary>All 40 player-season records · works without JavaScript</summary>
      <p>CPOE uses percentage points (pp); completion and sack avoidance use percent. D means recorded dropbacks; O combines D with recorded non-scramble runs. EPA means expected points added. Intervals are marginal conditional sensitivities, not tests of differences. Values below use display rounding; the downloadable data retain source precision.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="All 40 player-season records" tabindex="0">
        <table data-all-players><caption>Fixed 20-ID cohort, both seasons. Each metric cell names its denominator and uncertainty status.</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Passer / season</th><th scope="col">CPOE (pp)</th><th scope="col">Completion (%)</th><th scope="col">EPA / D</th><th scope="col">Sack avoidance (%)</th><th scope="col">Scramble EPA / O</th><th scope="col">Non-scramble EPA / O</th><th scope="col">Scramble usage / diagnostic</th><th scope="col">Non-scramble usage / diagnostic</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{data.rows.map(r=><tr><th scope="row">{r.observed_name}<br/>{r.season}<br/><small>{r.player_key}</small></th>
            {['cpoe_pp','completion_pct','epa_per_dropback','sack_avoidance_pct','scramble_contribution','nonscramble_contribution'].map(f=><td><strong>{fmt(r[f])}</strong><br/>{evidence(r,f)}<br/><small>{interval(r,f)}</small></td>)}
            {['scramble','nonscramble'].map(tag=><td>{r[`${tag}_runs`]} runs in {r[`${tag}_games`]} games<br/>{fmt(r[`${tag}_share_pct`])}% of {r.combined_opportunities} O in {r.combined_games} games<br/>{fmt(r[`${tag}_epa_per_run`])} EPA / role run<br/><small>{String(r[`${tag}_role_mean_status`]).replaceAll('_',' ')}; no share/per-run intervals</small></td>)}
          </tr>)}</tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="complete-table"><summary>All 10 study rows · works without JavaScript</summary>
      <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="All ten study associations" tabindex="0"><table data-all-studies>
        <caption>Approximate 95% conditional working-model sensitivities. Annual CPOE uses full-estimate centering; sack/run studies center each season on its own replicate mean. Games are deletion/sampling units. Annual strata contain 223 + 208 games where reported; these are not 431 independent quarterback pairs. Approximate game independence remains a working assumption.</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Study</th><th scope="col">Estimate</th><th scope="col">Interval</th><th scope="col">Actors / contributing games</th><th scope="col">Status / influence</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{data.study_associations.map(s=><tr><th scope="row">{studyLabel(s)}</th><td>{fmt(s.estimate)}</td><td>{fmt(s.lower)} to {fmt(s.upper)}</td><td>{s.cohort_count} passers; {s.contributing_games ?? 'game count not in base export'}</td><td>{s.status.replaceAll('_',' ')}{s.point_status && <span>; point: {s.point_status}</span>}{s.influence && <p>Game-deletion r: {fmt(s.influence.game_deletion_min)} to {fmt(s.influence.game_deletion_max)} ({s.influence.game_undefined} undefined). Passer-deletion r: {fmt(s.influence.actor_deletion_min)} to {fmt(s.influence.actor_deletion_max)} ({s.influence.actor_undefined} undefined; {s.influence.actor_sign_reversals} sign reversals).</p>}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table></div>
    </details>
    <noscript><p>The complete 40-record and ten-study tables above work without JavaScript. Open their headings to inspect the evidence. Switching charts requires JavaScript.</p></noscript>
    <p class="download"><a href={DATA_URL} download>Download the reviewed aggregate data</a> · <a href={MANIFEST_URL}>Data manifest</a></p>
  </section>
</nfl-comparison>
<script>
  import {registerNFL} from '../lib/nfl-charts';
  registerNFL();
</script>
<style>
  nfl-comparison {display:block;margin-block:var(--space-l);min-width:0;}
  h2,h3 {margin-block:0 var(--space-s);}
  p {max-width:65ch;}
  .scope,.control-note,figcaption,caption,.unit,.plot-note,.download {font-size:var(--type-small);}
  .availability {border-block:var(--rule) solid var(--green);padding-block:var(--space-s);}
  .player-controls,.shared-controls {display:grid;gap:var(--space-s);margin-block:var(--space-m);}
  label {display:grid;gap:var(--space-2xs);min-width:0;}
  select,button {width:100%;min-height:44px;min-width:0;padding:var(--space-2xs);font:inherit;color:var(--green);background:var(--cream);border:var(--rule) solid var(--green);border-radius:0;}
  select:disabled {opacity:1;border-style:dashed;}
  button {width:auto;cursor:pointer;}
  :is(select,button,summary,.table-scroll):focus-visible {outline:var(--rule-thick) solid var(--accent);outline-offset:var(--space-3xs);}
  .comparison-figure {margin:var(--space-l) 0;}
  .identities {font-weight:600;}
  .unit {margin-bottom:var(--space-2xs);}
  .chart-host {width:100%;min-width:0;}
  svg {display:block;width:100%;height:auto;background:var(--sand);}
  svg[hidden],[hidden] {display:none;}
  svg :global(text) {fill:var(--green);font-family:var(--font-body);font-size:16px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;}
  svg :global(.tick) {font-family:var(--font-numeric);font-size:13px;}
  svg :global(.axis),svg :global(.grid) {stroke:var(--green);stroke-width:1;}
  svg :global(.grid) {stroke-opacity:.3;}
  svg :global(.reference) {stroke:var(--green);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:5 5;}
  svg :global(.interval),svg :global(.trajectory) {stroke-width:2.5;}
  svg :global(.series-a) {stroke:var(--green);}
  svg :global(.series-b) {stroke:var(--accent);}
  svg :global(.trajectory.series-b) {stroke-dasharray:6 4;}
  svg :global(.mark-a) {fill:var(--green);stroke:var(--cream);stroke-width:1;}
  svg :global(.mark-b) {fill:var(--sand);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2.5;}
  svg :global(.mark-cohort) {fill:var(--sand);stroke:var(--green);stroke-width:1.5;}
  svg :global(.label-leader) {stroke:var(--green);stroke-width:1;}
  svg :global(.cohort-interval) {stroke:var(--green);stroke-width:1;}
  svg :global(.composition-part) {stroke:var(--cream);stroke-width:1.5;}
  svg :global(.part-0) {fill:var(--green);}
  svg :global(.part-1) {fill:url(#sack-hatch);}
  svg :global(.part-2) {fill:var(--sand);stroke:var(--green);}
  svg :global(.part-3) {fill:url(#run-hatch);}
  svg :global(.pattern-ground) {fill:var(--cream);}
  svg :global(.pattern-line) {stroke:var(--green);stroke-width:2;}
  figcaption {margin-top:var(--space-s);max-width:65ch;}
  details {border-top:var(--rule) solid var(--green);padding-block:var(--space-s);margin-top:var(--space-m);}
  summary {cursor:pointer;min-height:44px;display:list-item;}
  .table-scroll {overflow-x:auto;max-width:100%;scrollbar-color:var(--green) var(--cream);}
  .table-scroll :global(table) {width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--type-small);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;}
  .table-scroll :global(caption) {text-align:left;padding-block:var(--space-s);max-width:65ch;}
  .table-scroll :global(th),.table-scroll :global(td) {text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:var(--space-xs);border-bottom:var(--rule-thin) solid var(--green);min-width:8rem;max-width:23rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere;}
  .table-scroll :global(th) {font-weight:600;}
  .table-scroll :global(small) {font-size:inherit;}
  .complete-table .table-scroll :global(td) {min-width:14rem;}
  .composition-key {display:none;}
  nfl-comparison[data-view="composition"] .composition-key {display:block;}
  @media(min-width:40rem) {.player-controls {grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));}.shared-controls {grid-template-columns:minmax(6rem,1fr) minmax(0,2fr) minmax(0,2fr);}}
  @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce) {svg {scroll-behavior:auto;}}
</style>
